WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.217
- I'm Governor Bobby Jindal,

00:00:02.217 --> 00:00:05.859
and I'm here to take on the
issues through push-ups.

00:00:06.849 --> 00:00:08.587
- [Voiceover] Coming to you live

00:00:08.587 --> 00:00:10.728
from the BuzzFeed
studios in the Big Apple,

00:00:10.728 --> 00:00:12.173
we're just moments away from

00:00:12.173 --> 00:00:15.229
putting politics to the push-up mat.

00:00:16.019 --> 00:00:18.307
Governor Bobby Jindal, in the building,

00:00:18.307 --> 00:00:19.345
ready to go.

00:00:19.345 --> 00:00:21.671
Let's see who he's up against.

00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:26.828
Taxes, his first foe.

00:00:26.828 --> 00:00:29.246
The governor's not a fan,
but if you don't pay em,

00:00:29.246 --> 00:00:30.698
you go to prison.

00:00:30.698 --> 00:00:32.994
You can ask Wesley Snipes.

00:00:32.994 --> 00:00:35.362
Obamacare coming off a huge win

00:00:35.362 --> 00:00:37.445
at the Supreme Court earlier this year.

00:00:37.445 --> 00:00:40.501
This battle is one to watch.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.300
The governor has said countless times

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.249
that he's tired of hyphenated Americans.

00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:48.588
Definitely no love lost here.

00:00:48.588 --> 00:00:51.635
And of course, the
fiercest challenger today,

00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:53.515
Governor Jindal's very own

00:00:53.515 --> 00:00:56.938
2009 State of the Union response speech.

00:00:56.938 --> 00:01:00.027
These two have history
and it's not pretty.

00:01:00.027 --> 00:01:01.154
(ringing bell)

00:01:01.154 --> 00:01:03.775
Let's go to the floor.

00:01:03.775 --> 00:01:05.157
- Now we're talking a lot today

00:01:05.157 --> 00:01:08.357
about 2009 State of the
Union response speech

00:01:08.357 --> 00:01:09.779
cause it was a tough one.

00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:11.455
Now do you think you're overlooking

00:01:11.455 --> 00:01:13.568
Obamacare and taxes today?

00:01:13.568 --> 00:01:14.858
- These are tough competitors.

00:01:14.858 --> 00:01:16.128
The stronger the taxes get,

00:01:16.128 --> 00:01:17.318
the less freedom we all have,

00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:19.157
so you can't overlook
either one of these two.

00:01:19.157 --> 00:01:21.035
- Wow, you heard that here first.

00:01:21.035 --> 00:01:22.662
So we're going to get
right to the competition.

00:01:22.662 --> 00:01:23.676
Are you ready?

00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:25.261
Do you need anything
like some gym clothes?

00:01:25.261 --> 00:01:26.510
- I'm good to go, let's go.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:27.506
- We're good to go.

00:01:27.506 --> 00:01:30.848
Let's put politics and
push-ups to the test.

00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:32.260
(ringing bell)

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.061
- [Voiceover] Competitors
down on your mats.

00:01:40.637 --> 00:01:45.609
Ready, get set, and go!

00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:50.609
(cheers)

00:01:57.967 --> 00:01:59.831
- [Voiceover] Taxes is down.

00:01:59.831 --> 00:02:04.250
Not a strong showing, but
hey, we'll see you next April.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:09.136
(heavy rock music)

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.806
- [Voiceover] And hyphenated
Americans hit the mat.

00:02:13.806 --> 00:02:15.507
Looks like the governor was right.

00:02:15.507 --> 00:02:19.607
We are all just Americans,
at least for today.

00:02:19.607 --> 00:02:22.563
Obamacare is out. Incredible!

00:02:22.563 --> 00:02:25.357
Absolutely shocking.

00:02:25.357 --> 00:02:27.155
Governor Jindal rolling back

00:02:27.155 --> 00:02:30.771
landmark legislation in under 30 push-ups.

00:02:30.771 --> 00:02:33.494
Two long time rivals.

00:02:33.494 --> 00:02:35.739
Mano a mano, neck and neck,

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:37.537
neither wants to give in.

00:02:37.537 --> 00:02:40.858
Neither want to show any weakness.

00:02:43.268 --> 00:02:45.634
What an effort from these two competitors.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:49.758
With every push, a grudging
respect growing between them.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.974
Incredible.

00:02:53.974 --> 00:02:55.386
The State of the Union response

00:02:55.386 --> 00:02:58.118
is pushing Jindal to keep going.

00:03:00.378 --> 00:03:02.436
The State of the Union response

00:03:02.436 --> 00:03:05.565
asking just one more
push-up from the governor.

00:03:05.565 --> 00:03:07.159
Just one more.

00:03:09.089 --> 00:03:13.245
And Oh! Jindal's knee is on the mat.

00:03:13.245 --> 00:03:15.317
Jindal's knee is on the mat!

00:03:15.317 --> 00:03:17.288
It's over! It's over!

00:03:17.288 --> 00:03:19.452
(chanting U.S.A.)

00:03:19.452 --> 00:03:21.494
- [Gov. Jindal] I think we can
finally put this behind us.

00:03:21.494 --> 00:03:22.876
I think America won today.

00:03:22.876 --> 00:03:27.876
(triumphant music)

